<SiteLayout title="Privacy · Historica" description="How Historica handles analytics, cookies, appearance preferences and links to other sites." path="/privacy" page="privacy">
<header><a href="/" class="brand">historica</a><span class="beta-sash">BETA</span><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Explore</a><a href="/about">About</a></nav><ThemeControl /></header>
<main class="about-page"><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="about-lead">You can explore Historica without an account. We don’t use advertising cookies or build profiles of the people who visit.</p>
<section><h2>Analytics</h2><p>When enabled on the live site, Cloudflare Web Analytics helps us understand which pages people visit and how well the site performs. It measures things such as page visits, loading times, browser type and broad geographical location. Analytics is not enabled on local or staging previews.</p><p>Cloudflare Web Analytics does not use cookies or browser storage to collect these metrics, and does not fingerprint individual visitors. Cloudflare says it does not log URL query strings. We do not add search terms, comparison selections or slider movements as custom tracking events.</p><p>Our configuration counts visits to loaded pages. Moving between histories within the explorer does not send an additional page-view event.</p><p>You can read more in Cloudflare’s <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/data-metrics/core-web-vitals/">analytics documentation</a> and <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/faq/">Web Analytics FAQ</a>.</p></section>
<section><h2>Cookies and your appearance preference</h2><p>Historica’s application does not set cookies. The moon button saves your choice of light or dark mode in this browser using local storage. That preference stays on your device; it is not sent to our analytics service.</p><p>You can remove the saved preference by clearing this site’s data in your browser. Without a saved choice, Historica follows your device’s appearance setting.</p></section>
<section><h2>Bookmarks and other websites</h2><p>The selected history, dates and other view settings are kept in the page address so you can bookmark or share them. Anyone you share that address with can see those settings.</p><p>Links to historical sources, GitHub and other websites take you to services with their own privacy policies. Those sites may use cookies.</p></section>
<section><h2>Hosting and questions</h2><p>Serving a website involves technical information such as your IP address and the address you request. Hosting and network providers may process that information to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. Cookie-free analytics does not mean that no technical data is processed.</p><p>Historica is created by Ian Sproates. For questions about this page, you can contact me through <a href="https://sproates.net">my website</a>.</p></section>
<footer><a href="/coverage.html">Sources and research coverage</a> · <a href="/privacy" aria-current="page">Privacy</a><p>Historica is an open source site on <a href="https://github.com/sproates/historica">GitHub</a>.</p></footer></main>
</SiteLayout>
